From 4e989a3ceadaa5fb55200bea795a933efed3d768 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 21:09:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02434/11362] [outer-loop] tr87 extended to L4:
 double_translation 2-pass rewrite chain

Operator: push on to L4. RE'd the L4 delta from internal state + the win predicate.

L4 sets double_translation=True. The rules now form a two-level CHAIN across three
glyph series: A->B (A6->B1, A1->B3, ...) AND B->C (B1->C3, B3->C2, ...) both live
in cifzvbcuwqe. The target is A-series, the editable is C-series, so the win = the
editable matches the target rewritten TWICE (A->B->C). Confirmed empirically: a
2-pass greedy rewrite of the target wins L4.

Generalized required_editable to apply the greedy rewrite N PASSES, where N=2 if
tree_translation OR double_translation is set on the level (read via
game.current_level.get_data), else 1. One function now spans L1-L4: 1-to-1,
1-to-many, many-to-many (1 pass) and the 2-pass chain.

- solve_adaptered('tr87',4) -> reached_level=4, offline_reproduced=True (81 actions,
  319 states). cyclic-distance verifier + fresh_env carry over unchanged.
- 9 adapter unit tests (synthetic game now tag-based with level flags + a 3-series
  chain for the L4 2-pass case; the no-flag control gives nonzero distance); all pass.
- metaharness 81-action replay -> L4; aggregate now 30 levels / 16 games (was 29/16).
- tr87 is 4 of 6 levels. Registry: L4 mechanic + the L5-L6 boundary recorded (likely
  alter_rules -- the rules themselves become editable; the N-pass rewrite returns
  None->1000 there so the search stops at L4 with no false claim).

L5 RE (the alter_rules editing semantics) is the documented next step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
